{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Split implemented on branch split-workflow-executor (commit 74daf58e52).\n\nConcern boundary as planned: the step-kind I/O CONTRACT MODEL moved to\nsrc/rebar/llm/workflow/step_contracts.py; the RUN ENGINE stayed in executor.py.\n\nSizes: executor.py 790 -> 656 LOC (144 lines of headroom, below the 720 near-cap band);\nstep_contracts.py 181 LOC (over the 100-LOC floor). No src/rebar file exceeds the cap and\n.github/module-size-limit.txt is byte-identical to origin/main.\n\nMoved bodies verified byte-identical to their originals (StepContract + STEP_CONTRACTS,\ncontract_for, input_schema_for, and the whole shallow-check section).\n\nGates: make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (574 files);\nscripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check -> active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0 (run\ndirectly, not just via make lint, because make lint tolerates stale=1 and CI does not);\ntests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py 79 passed; scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py clean;\nruff --select C901 clean on both files.\n\nTests: 751 passed across tests/unit/workflow, test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam,\ntest_llm_seam_clean_heldout, test_workflow_scripted_steps, test_reuse_surface_doc and\ntest_core_optionality. No test assertion, fixture, import or expected value changed.\n\nPath-keyed registries checked and their outcome:\n- tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py _MARKER_BUDGET pins llm/workflow/executor.py\n  to exactly one '# read-via:' line. The expression resolver that carries it deliberately\n  stayed, so the budget is untouched and GREEN.\n- tests/unit/workflow/test_executor_tripwire.py scans executor.py + interpreter.py for banned\n  imports and the Burr trigger-list prose. The moved cluster has no control flow and no\n  imports and the docstring stayed, so the tripwire needed no change.\n- .github/complexity-baseline.json has zero entries keyed to llm/workflow/executor.py, so no\n  baselined symbol was relocated (checked before choosing the seam).\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam.py carried two stale <file>:<line> prose\n  citations (executor.py:155 -> :166 for STEP_REGISTRY, executor.py:673-676 -> :539-542 for\n  the registry lookup). Both repointed under the plan's bounded exception: one docstring, one\n  assertion MESSAGE, no assertion touched.\n- No module census / allowlist enumerates src/rebar/llm/workflow modules, so the new file\n  needed no registry entry.\n\nReference sweep done BOTH ways: Serena find_referencing_symbols on shallow_contract_check,\ninput_schema_for, contract_for and StepContract, then a plain grep for all nine moved names as\nstrings across *.py and *.md. The two sets agree; the four in-src lazy import sites were\nrepointed at step_contracts and executor re-exports StepContract / STEP_CONTRACTS /\ncontract_for / shallow_contract_check so every existing import point resolves unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787189025663461001,"uuid":"461e7b1c-ca4d-4119-bbd5-674b77405eb7"}